# .graphifyignore — what stays OUT of the kit's knowledge graph (graphify, AST only, zero API).
#
# gitignore syntax, negation with `!` included. One criterion: the graph exists to answer
# STRUCTURAL questions (who defines / calls what, direct radius of a change). Process history,
# generated views and agent tooling only dilute the hubs and inflate every query.
#
# What the graph KEEPS (never filter):
#   bin/sdd            · the runner — bash functions and their DIRECT statement calls
#   agents/*.md        · the agent contracts
#   tests/*.sh         · the sensors (functions + direct calls)
#   templates/*.md     · the artifact contracts
#   config/            · schema and starter config
#   docs/pipeline.md docs/failure-modes.md docs/adr/*.md docs/graphify.md
#   CLAUDE.md README.md CONTEXT.md
#
# Measured zone for bash (2026-09-01, docs/graphify.md § Competence zone): the extractor sees
# function DEFINITIONS and calls written as a statement (`f args`, `if f; then`, `f || rc=$?`).
# It does NOT see `$(f)` command substitution, dynamic dispatch (`gate_"$phase"`), and it collapses
# N call sites of one pair into ONE edge — so it never answers a door census. Orientation only.

# ── Runner state, logs, agent tooling ───────────────────────────────────────
.sdd/**
.claude/**
.superpowers/**
.github/**
graphify-out/**

# ── Process history: handoffs, QA tree, specs, backlog, kaizen log ──────────
# Valuable to people, noise to a dependency graph: a 2026-08-17 review round outranked
# config/schema.md on a query about the REVIEW budget when these were indexed (measured).
docs/handoffs/**
docs/qa/**
docs/superpowers/**
TODO.md
KAIZEN_LOG.md

# ── Fixtures and text data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/fixtures/**
tests/*.txt
